{"claims":[{"claim_text":"Republicans will uphold and defend the party's core principles: constraining the federal government to its legitimate constitutional functions, empowering people while limiting its reach into their lives, spending only what is necessary, and taxing only to raise revenue for essential government functions.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Republicans will unleash the power of enterprise, innovation, civic energy, and the American spirit, and will not pretend that government is a substitute for family or community.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The other party wants more government control over people's lives and earnings; Republicans do not.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"The other party wants to continue pork barrel politics; Republicans are disgusted by it, no matter who practices it.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"The other party wants to ignore fiscal problems while squandering billions on ineffective programs; Republicans are determined to end that waste.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Republicans will confront and ultimately defeat the entrenched culture of official Washington, which is an intrusive tax-and-spend liberalism.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"The federal government collects $2.7 trillion a year from American families and businesses, which is $7.4 billion a day.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[4]},{"claim_text":"The federal government spends over $3 trillion a year, which is $8.2 billion a day.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[4]},{"claim_text":"Those who created the bloated federal government will not admit a single mistake or abolish a single program.", "claim_types":["characterization"],"evidence_ids":[4]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

